[[63,7,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p>1. Use a spanner on the moving tensioner (1a) and remove the engine\ncomponents single drive belt (1b).</p><p>2. Undo the nuts (2a) and remove the water pump (2b) complete with\ngasket.</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2066327.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[63,7,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"removing\" data-part=\"removal\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"refitting\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</a><p><a href=\"#/2585279\">1004D40</a></p><p><a href=\"#/2585294\">1032B16</a></p><p>1. Use the tool to prevent the pulley from turning.</p><p>2. Unscrew retaining bolt (2a) and remove pulley (2b) from its seat\non the camshaft.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001268.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Country</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1</p></td><td><p>Support for counter-torque</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.860.831.000</p></td></tr></table></div><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001268.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Country</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1</p></td><td><p>Support for counter-torque</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.860.831.000</p></td></tr></table></div><p>3. Unscrew the retaining bolts</p><p>4. Remove coolant pump (4a) with its underlying O-ring (4b).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2022385.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[63,7,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>1. Place the water pump (1a), complete with gasket, back in its\nhousing and secure it tightening the bolts (1b) to the recommended\ntorque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>1b</p></td><td><p>Nut</p></td><td><p>COOLANT PUMP</p></td><td><p>M6</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>(Upper engine crankcase side) 0.8 ÷ 1.0</p></td></tr></table></div><p>2. Use a spanner on the moving tensioner (2a) and fit the single\ndrive belt (2b).</p><figure class=\"photo\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2066328.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure>"],[63,7,0,"<h3 class=\"step\" data-step=\"refitting\" data-part=\"refit\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/21.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Refitting</h3><a class=\"jump\" href=\"#\" data-jump=\"removing\"><img class=\"icon\" src=\"../media/20.jpg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\">Removing</a><p>Replace the O-ring before fitting the coolant\npump.</p><p>Fit the coolant pump and tighten the bolts\nto torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>COOLANT PUMP</p></td><td><p>M8</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>2.5</p></td></tr></table></div><p>Fit the pulley into its seat on the camshaft.</p><p>Tighten the bolt and lock the pulley using\nthe tool. Then tighten the pulley  bolt to torque.</p><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001268.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Country</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Support for counter-torque</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.860.831.000</p></td></tr></table></div><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001268.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Name</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Country</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Support for counter-torque</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>1.860.831.000</p></td></tr></table></div><div class=\"table\"><table><tr><th><figure class=\"diagram\"><img class=\"zoomable\" src=\"../media/2001243.svg\" alt=\"\" loading=\"lazy\"></figure></th><th><p>Fastening</p></th><th><p>Component</p></th><th><p>Ø</p></th><th colspan=\"1\"><p>Value</p><p>(daNm)</p></th></tr><tr><td><p>-</p></td><td><p>Bolt</p></td><td><p>TIMING GEAR DRIVEN PULLEYS</p></td><td><p>M12</p></td><td colspan=\"1\"><p>12</p></td></tr></table></div><p><a href=\"#/2585294\">1032B16</a></p><p><a href=\"#/2585279\">1004D40</a></p>"]]